# Semgrep's built-in default ignore rules exclude any directory named
# test/ or tests/ (see semgrep/templates/.semgrepignore in the semgrep
# package) — that's a real problem for us: a target repo's own test/
# directory is exactly the kind of place a hardcoded secret or an unsafe
# eval() ends up, and it's also where Nettle's own scanner test fixtures
# live (test/fixtures/...), so the built-in default silently skipped both.
# This file exists so semgrep uses it (even mostly-empty) instead of
# falling back to those defaults — see semgrepScanner.ts's execFileSync
# `cwd` option, which points here specifically so this file is always
# found regardless of where the actual scan target lives.
#
# Only exclude what's genuinely not source code worth scanning.
node_modules/
.git/
dist/
build/
.venv/
.tox/
*.min.js
